---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const formUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_APPLY_FORM_URL_EN ?? '#';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base lang="en" title="Apply — TailorMind">
  <h1>Apply</h1>

  <h2>From your terminal, with your agent</h2>
  <p>This is the main path, and there is nothing to install:</p>
  <pre class="not-prose"><code>git clone https://github.com/Tailor-Mind/tm-dev-challenge
cd tm-dev-challenge
claude            # or whichever assistant you use
/tm-apply</code></pre>
  <p>The repo ships the skill, so your agent sees it the moment it opens. It will ask for your details and for the <strong>specification you would start the challenge with</strong> — the part we actually read — and hand you your key. Keep it: without it no run opens.</p>
  <p>Using a different assistant? Open <code>.claude/skills/tm-apply/SKILL.md</code> for it and ask it to follow that. It is a text file with a <code>curl</code> in it; nothing proprietary.</p>

  <h2>Or through the form</h2>
  <p>It costs you nothing and we confirm every application by email. But the job is directing agents, so which door you come through says something about how you work — and we note it.</p>
  <p>Submit the form below. We acknowledge every application by email.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Upload your CV (PDF).</li>
    <li>Provide your LinkedIn URL.</li>
    <li>Answer two short reasoning questions — calibrated, not graded for "correctness".</li>
    <li>Choose your preferred language for further communication.</li>
    <li><strong>Complete the take-home — it is required.</strong> Leave the "Take-home repo URL" field blank for now. After submitting, you'll get a confirmation email with an <strong>edit link</strong> — come back, complete the <a href={`${b}/en/take-home/`}>take-home</a>, then reopen the form via that link and paste your repo URL. We record elapsed time from first submit to URL paste.</li>
  </ol>
  {formUrl !== '#'
    ? <p class="not-prose">
        <a href={formUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="inline-block px-5 py-3 rounded bg-[color:var(--color-brand-600)] text-white font-medium">
          Open application form ↗
        </a>
        <span class="block text-sm text-zinc-500 mt-2">Opens in a new tab (Google Forms — the CV upload step requires it).</span>
      </p>
    : <p class="not-prose p-4 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-300 rounded">Google Form URL not configured yet. Set <code>PUBLIC_APPLY_FORM_URL_EN</code>.</p>}
  <h2>The take-home is required</h2>
  <p>No application moves to the interview without a submitted take-home. It is not optional and not a tie-breaker: it is Stage 2 of the process, scored on the same rubric as the interview.</p>
  <p>What is up to you is the <em>when</em>: submit it now (paste the repo URL in the form and your application moves to the take-home-submitted state) or wait until we've screened your CV and explicitly ask for it (~5 business days). We won't penalize either path. If we reject on CV we won't evaluate the take-home, but we'll tell you within ~5 days so you don't keep wondering.</p>
  <p><strong>Ship what you actually reviewed.</strong> Use any LLM you like — that is the point — but read your deliverable before publishing it. If content shows up that isn't part of the spec, we read that as no final review.</p>

  <p>Data handling: see <a href={`${b}/en/privacy/`}>privacy</a>.</p>
</Base>
